sentations may not yet show these findings."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Biliary Obstruction Source of Acute Abdominal Pain", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.077, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of jaundice or lab evidence of obstruction moderately argues against biliary obstruction as the primary mechanism."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Pancreatic Source of Acute Abdominal Pain", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.051, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Classic pancreatic pain patterns (epigastric/back radiation) are absent, moderately reducing likelihood despite alcohol abuse as a risk factor."]}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do daily alcohol consumption and rapid weight loss (Budd-Chiari risk factors) combined with acute RUQ pain strongly support a hepatic vascular source?", "summary": "Alcohol abuse and rapid weight loss are recognized risk factors for Budd-Chiari syndrome, providing moderate support for hepatic/vascular sources despite missing typical physical findings."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the diffuse RUQ tenderness and history of unprotected sex (possible cholangitis risk) support common bile duct obstruction as the primary mechanism?", "summary": "Unprotected sex as a potential cholangitis risk factor is weakly linked to biliary obstruction, but absence of obstructive symptoms (jaundice, epigastric pain) reduces its plausibility."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the right upper quadrant (RUQ) emphasis of pain argue against a g